*** Charter

**** General

*!This is a first draft.!*

The Project is seperated in two areas.

1. Data provision by aimediq and Bitmos (getting the data into the cloud)

2. Data integration on the side of Noahlabs (creating and providing ReOxy dashboards for COVIVID app)

In order to not blow the scope This Charter outlines only this Pilot Project with covivid.


**** Goal & Scope

Inclusion of the ReOxy data into Noahlabs API (COVIVID app) API.
Provisioning of the Data to the COVIVID app users to the satisfaction of COVIVID
Creating positive Revenue or a profitable outcome for the  involved Parties
while keeping cost and scope low with potential for extension of capabilities and cooperation.

**** Limit

For now the scope would be limited to COVIVID as a pilot Project. The ReOxy data will not be analyzed by AI.

Data from the Patients will be handled after regulations and guidelines. Since Noahlabs knows this area better they
will advise.

There will be no changes to the Hardware of any device for this Project. Aimediqs advance to interface via Lan
or other means is a seperate project. One exeption may GDPR update from aimediq.
(Upgrade to SSD and Operator Credentials) this could prove beneficial to the Project but is handled on the side of
aimediq.

Avoid changes to the raw data that impact the functionality of the COVIVID app provided by noahlabs after the integration.
Smaller adjustments can be negotiated between the parties. Since advancement in this area are quick and
might impact either side i have covered this in the Risk analysis section.

No Changes to the data and or dashboards requested by COVIVID during the Project unless mutually agreed upon.
There is a high risk of this blowing the scope.

**** Buisness Case

Mr Weiss specifically asked for

- the number of devices in germany
- Projection of ReOxy sales in Germany
- International Activity
- Projection of international sales
  
**** Napkin Math

since nearly all users of the ReOxy in Germany operate the devices at high capacity the number of patients
treated should be displayed as well. Ulrike told me she has about 100 Treatments per Week in her office alone(2 devices).

In flechtingen 3(devices) they had around 900 Patients last year. Averaging 25 patients per device per month

those are probably the highest "output" locations

Our partners at Covivd have 13 devices at the moment. 3 more are are planned. However they also do more treatments
per patient then Flechtingen and one less per week, impacting the calculation. I tried to be moderate.

I Estimated about 175 patients per month at COVIVID.
(this is a Napkin Math with additional 20% contingency and a guess...
I will collect some more data on mask sales for 2023 and make a better calculation.)

**** Case

  At Covivid there are currently 13 ReOxys deployed since Feb 2023. 3 more are alreaady in a concrete planning phase. 
  About 175 patients treated per month at COVIVID.

  Patients frequently ask for their ReOxy data. While the ReOxy data could be provided it is a hassle to do so,
  additionally providing the Treatment graphs and data currently cannot provide a good analysis that
  the patient can understand.

  NoahLabs app and the offered devices meet the medical standard and are novel. They would allow
  valuable data for the patient as they can monitor evident and easy to unbderstand parameters
  (Resting Heart Rate and BP as well as questionairs). They can also provide relevant infos for the
  doctor in a convinient way.

  Introduction of the devices offered by Noahlabs for monitoring treatment process as well as providing a 
  convienient way for patients and doctors to acees Treatment data would add Value to the ReOxy, and solve a challenge.

  The Question of the Patient ("Have I gotten better") can be answered by the docor by a click on a buttin
  using the noahlabs app. More Explicitly

  *"did i get better" would be answered with per ex. "your resting HR improved by x amount"
  "your BP improved" Your overall wellbeing has improved.*
  
  In turn that would mean if the Patient or Doctor wants a convinient way to acess the data, Noahlabs would be
  the Provider and would become an integral part of data Distribution to the docors and the Patient when using the ReOxy.

  *if you want patient reports we have a partner for that!*
  
  In short: If the Patient wants to know how they improved by using ReOxy the app and devices from noahlabs
  offer a evidence based easy to use novel solution.

  This would also open up possibilities to monitor further evidence based approaches in Cardiac Rehab.
  Per ex we have seen significant improvements in 6mwt in several modalities with ReOxy. incl. COVID19
  Measuring those end points through the app would be one idea of many.


